        "title": "Sports Psychology: Flow, Motivation, and Anxiety",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Sports psychology is applied cognitive and social psychology constrained by extreme performance conditions. The core problems: managing arousal so it optimizes rather than impairs performance, sustaining motivation over years of training, maintaining attention under pressure, and building the mental resilience to recover from failure. The science has both strong theoretical foundations (flow, self-efficacy, goal-setting) and practical intervention repertoires used with elite athletes."
